1
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:14,790
Fall back!

2
00:01:01,950 --> 00:01:03,070
Brother?

3
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:27,560
Did you send the ravens?

4
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:33,660
Tarly, look at me.

5
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:38,700
Did you send the ravens?

6
00:02:42,970 --> 00:02:44,770
That was your job.

7
00:02:45,670 --> 00:02:47,410
Your only job.

8
00:02:55,540 --> 00:02:57,410
We need to get back to the Wall.

9
00:02:59,090 --> 00:03:00,550
It's a long march.

10
00:03:01,490 --> 00:03:03,090
We know what's out there,

11
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:07,310
but we have to make it, have to warn them

12
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:10,360
or before winter's done,

13
00:03:11,030 --> 00:03:14,790
everyone you've ever known will be dead.

14
00:06:08,420 --> 00:06:10,470
First time you've seen a giant, Jon Snow?

15
00:06:13,980 --> 00:06:16,060
Well, don't stare too long. They're shy.

16
00:06:18,810 --> 00:06:21,680
When they stop being shy, they get angry.

17
00:06:22,210 --> 00:06:23,640
And when they're angry,

18
00:06:24,270 --> 00:06:27,290
I've seen them pound a man straight into the ground

19
00:06:27,290 --> 00:06:28,960
like a hammer on a nail.

20
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:42,090
Crow! Crow!

21
00:06:42,090 --> 00:06:43,850
- Look over there! - Crow!

22
00:06:45,210 --> 00:06:47,690
Crow! Look over here! Look!

23
00:06:47,970 --> 00:06:50,100
Ah, look, crow coming!

24
00:06:51,010 --> 00:06:52,110
Crow!

25
00:06:54,690 --> 00:06:56,320
You're wearing the wrong color.

26
00:06:58,130 --> 00:06:59,680
Mance was a ranger.

27
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:04,590
In your hearts, all you crows want to fly free.

28
00:07:04,590 --> 00:07:06,490
When I'm free, will I be free to go?

29
00:07:06,490 --> 00:07:07,830
- Crow! - Crow!

30
00:07:07,840 --> 00:07:09,060
Sure, you will.

31
00:07:12,490 --> 00:07:14,410
And I'll be free to kill you.

32
00:07:16,470 --> 00:07:18,270
Got no respect, this lot.

33
00:07:18,840 --> 00:07:21,490
Got no fathers to slap 'em when they're foul.

34
00:07:22,280 --> 00:07:24,010
What happened to their fathers?

35
00:07:25,830 --> 00:07:28,280
Some of them were killed by crows like you.

36
00:07:30,140 --> 00:07:32,480
Don't look so grim, Jon Snow.

37
00:07:33,080 --> 00:07:36,000
If Mance Rayder likes you, you'll live another day.

38
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,500
And if he don't...

39
00:08:01,660 --> 00:08:03,330
I smell a crow.

40
00:08:03,330 --> 00:08:04,880
We killed his friends.

41
00:08:05,520 --> 00:08:07,460
Thought you'd want to question this one.

42
00:08:08,380 --> 00:08:10,490
What do we want with a baby crow?

43
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:12,990
This baby killed Qhorin Halfhand.

44
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:15,780
He wants to be one of us.

45
00:08:22,450 --> 00:08:25,580
That half-handed cunt killed friends of mine.

46
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:27,710
Friends twice your size.

47
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:33,110
My father told me big men fall just as quick as little ones

48
00:08:33,460 --> 00:08:35,790
if you put a sword through their hearts.

49
00:08:37,570 --> 00:08:42,570
Plenty of little men tried to put their swords through my heart.

50
00:08:42,710 --> 00:08:47,070
And there's plenty of little skeletons buried in the woods.

51
00:08:49,170 --> 00:08:51,670
- What's your name, boy? - Jon Snow.

52
00:08:58,340 --> 00:08:59,700
Your Grace.

53
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:04,410
Your Grace?

54
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:07,280
Did you hear that?

55
00:09:07,300 --> 00:09:10,730
From now on, you'd better kneel every time I fart.

56
00:09:11,620 --> 00:09:13,230
Stand, boy.

57
00:09:15,570 --> 00:09:18,560
We don't kneel for anyone beyond the Wall.

58
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:25,490
So, you're Ned Stark's bastard.

59
00:09:26,550 --> 00:09:28,770
Thank you for the gift, Lord of Bones.

60
00:09:28,770 --> 00:09:30,190
You can leave us.

61
00:09:40,020 --> 00:09:41,490
The girl likes you.

62
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:43,610
You like her back, Snow?

63
00:09:44,130 --> 00:09:45,940
That why you want to join us?

64
00:09:46,330 --> 00:09:48,210
Don't panic, boy.

65
00:09:48,260 --> 00:09:50,300
This isn't the damned Night's Watch

66
00:09:50,300 --> 00:09:52,900
where we make you swear off girls.

67
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:56,520
This chicken eater you thought was king is Tormund Giantsbane.

68
00:09:56,520 --> 00:10:00,630
Can't believe this pup killed the Halfhand.

69
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:02,800
He was our enemy

70
00:10:03,380 --> 00:10:05,410
and I'm glad he's dead.

71
00:10:15,910 --> 00:10:18,070
He was my brother once.

72
00:10:18,950 --> 00:10:21,160
Back when he had a whole hand.

73
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:24,450
What were you doing with him?

74
00:10:25,570 --> 00:10:27,840
The Lord Commander sent me to the Halfhand for seasoning.

75
00:10:27,990 --> 00:10:29,160
Why?

76
00:10:30,270 --> 00:10:31,910
He wants me to lead one day.

77
00:10:31,910 --> 00:10:35,050
But here you are, a traitor

78
00:10:35,180 --> 00:10:37,720
kneeling before the King-beyond-the-Wall.

79
00:10:38,020 --> 00:10:41,720
If I'm a traitor, then you are, too.

80
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:51,430
Why do you want to join us, Jon Snow?

81
00:10:58,060 --> 00:10:59,610
I want to be free.

82
00:10:59,980 --> 00:11:03,030
No, I don't think so.

83
00:11:04,130 --> 00:11:06,540
I think what you want most of all

84
00:11:06,720 --> 00:11:08,480
is to be a hero.

85
00:11:09,350 --> 00:11:11,950
I'll ask you one last time--

86
00:11:12,730 --> 00:11:14,910
why do you want to join us?

87
00:11:20,380 --> 00:11:23,080
We stopped at Craster's Keep on the way north.

88
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:26,430
I saw...

89
00:11:27,900 --> 00:11:29,000
You saw what?

90
00:11:31,460 --> 00:11:33,710
I saw Craster take his own baby boy

91
00:11:33,710 --> 00:11:35,240
and leave it in the woods.

92
00:11:36,460 --> 00:11:38,240
I saw what took it.

93
00:11:42,340 --> 00:11:46,340
You're telling me you saw one of them?

94
00:11:49,090 --> 00:11:51,590
And why would that make you desert your brothers?

95
00:11:52,190 --> 00:11:54,340
Because when I told the Lord Commander,

96
00:11:54,890 --> 00:11:56,330
he already knew.

97
00:11:58,470 --> 00:12:01,440
Thousands of years ago, the First Men

98
00:12:01,450 --> 00:12:04,170
battled the White Walkers and defeated them.

99
00:12:04,850 --> 00:12:08,810
I want to fight for the side that fights for the living.

100
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:13,740
Did I come to the right place?

101
00:12:19,140 --> 00:12:21,430
We'll need to find you a new cloak.

102
00:12:42,780 --> 00:12:44,850
What if you took off that bit there?

103
00:12:47,640 --> 00:12:50,630
Don't you want to leave something to the imagination?

104
00:12:50,720 --> 00:12:54,460
Trouble is, I've never had much imagination.

105
00:12:57,320 --> 00:12:59,140
I want you to take it off.

106
00:13:06,070 --> 00:13:07,190
Mouth.

107
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:16,560
Ser Bronn. Ser Bronn.

108
00:13:18,730 --> 00:13:20,300
I didn't hear that.

109
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:22,400
- Apologies, Ser. - Back away.

110
00:13:22,670 --> 00:13:25,540
Keep backing away till you're outside this establishment.

111
00:13:25,540 --> 00:13:28,870
- Then back away some more. - Lord Tyrion sent me.

112
00:13:29,300 --> 00:13:31,680
I will murder you, boy.

113
00:13:32,280 --> 00:13:34,680
He said it was a matter of life and death.

114
00:13:51,550 --> 00:13:54,620
- Pod? - It's your sister.

115
00:13:56,010 --> 00:13:57,340
The queen.

116
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:12,420
What are they doing here?

117
00:14:12,420 --> 00:14:13,920
Protecting me, I assume.

118
00:14:13,920 --> 00:14:15,820
Will you let me in?

119
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:18,630
No, I don't think so.

120
00:14:18,630 --> 00:14:21,900
If I wanted to kill you, do you think I'd let a wooden door stop me?

121
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:30,470
They stay outside.

122
00:14:30,470 --> 00:14:32,720
I'm not afraid of you, little brother.

123
00:14:47,870 --> 00:14:50,660
- Why are you here? - I wanted to see your face.

124
00:14:51,380 --> 00:14:52,730
They said you'd lost your nose,

125
00:14:52,730 --> 00:14:54,770
but it's not as gruesome as all that.

126
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:58,060
The man who cut me lost more than his nose.

127
00:14:58,060 --> 00:14:59,530
I should hope so.

128
00:15:00,590 --> 00:15:03,970
The rebels came for Joffrey's head, they lost their own.

129
00:15:04,010 --> 00:15:05,430
Thanks to Father.

130
00:15:06,410 --> 00:15:08,070
Thanks to Father.

131
00:15:09,810 --> 00:15:12,150
Of course, it wasn't a rebel who tried to kill me.

132
00:15:12,150 --> 00:15:14,110
No? Curious.

133
00:15:14,740 --> 00:15:18,250
Bit of a comedown from chamber of the Hand.

134
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:20,480
But then I don't suppose you need much room.

135
00:15:20,980 --> 00:15:23,510
Grand Maester Pycelle made the same joke.

136
00:15:23,510 --> 00:15:25,890
You must be proud to be as funny as

137
00:15:25,890 --> 00:15:27,210
a man whose balls brush his knees.

138
00:15:27,210 --> 00:15:28,840
You're meeting Father today?

139
00:15:29,980 --> 00:15:31,160
How do you know that?

140
00:15:31,160 --> 00:15:33,970
Because I have hundreds of spies in my employ.

141
00:15:34,190 --> 00:15:37,260
The Master of Whisperers owes me a favor or two.

142
00:15:39,070 --> 00:15:41,830
Father told me. What do you want from him?

143
00:15:42,100 --> 00:15:43,980
What do I want from him? He's my father.

144
00:15:43,990 --> 00:15:45,660
Do I need to want something?

145
00:15:48,770 --> 00:15:50,760
I'm sure he loves me dearly,

146
00:15:50,950 --> 00:15:54,150
as any father loves his child, his baby boy.

147
00:15:55,540 --> 00:15:59,290
Yet he hasn't come to visit once since arriving in King's Landing.

148
00:15:59,290 --> 00:16:02,680
I lay here, my face split in half,

149
00:16:03,010 --> 00:16:04,630
but Father never came.

150
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:11,810
You're going to make me cry.

151
00:16:12,410 --> 00:16:14,270
Why do you care what I want from him?

152
00:16:15,980 --> 00:16:18,410
Because you've slandered me to Father before.

153
00:16:18,410 --> 00:16:20,660
Slandered? When?

154
00:16:20,660 --> 00:16:22,420
You told him I had my guards

155
00:16:22,430 --> 00:16:24,770
beat that servant girl at Casterly Rock.

156
00:16:24,770 --> 00:16:26,530
You did have your guards beat her.

157
00:16:26,530 --> 00:16:27,950
A girl of nine, I believe.

158
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:29,480
I was nine, too.

159
00:16:29,740 --> 00:16:31,950
She lost an eye, if I remember correctly.

160
00:16:31,950 --> 00:16:33,110
If I remember correctly,

161
00:16:33,110 --> 00:16:35,040
she never stole a necklace again.

162
00:16:37,410 --> 00:16:40,150
It's not slander if it's true.

163
00:16:40,150 --> 00:16:42,840
And what's this truth you plan on telling him today?

164
00:16:42,880 --> 00:16:46,750
Why are you so nervous about what I'm going to say to Father?

165
00:16:46,760 --> 00:16:48,300
Because you're a liar.

166
00:16:49,100 --> 00:16:52,050
I expect you'll tell lies about me, about Joffrey.

167
00:16:52,300 --> 00:16:54,320
Any lies in particular?

168
00:16:56,250 --> 00:16:57,750
You're a clever man,

169
00:16:58,970 --> 00:17:01,100
but you're not half as clever as you think you are.

170
00:17:01,300 --> 00:17:03,230
Still makes me more clever than you.

171
00:17:07,730 --> 00:17:11,270
Oh, look at these two shining warriors.

172
00:17:11,270 --> 00:17:14,180
Ser Taryn Mant and...

173
00:17:14,590 --> 00:17:16,270
Ser Whosit of Whocares.

174
00:17:16,270 --> 00:17:17,950
Ser Meryn Trant.

175
00:17:17,970 --> 00:17:20,180
Ser Bronn of the Blackwater.

176
00:17:20,180 --> 00:17:22,400
- You're no knight. - Pod.

177
00:17:22,790 --> 00:17:26,280
Ser Bronn of the Blackwater was anointed by the king himself.

178
00:17:26,280 --> 00:17:28,910
You're an up-jumped cutthroat,

179
00:17:29,360 --> 00:17:30,510
nothing more.

180
00:17:30,510 --> 00:17:32,400
That's exactly who I am.

181
00:17:32,540 --> 00:17:34,860
And you're a grub in fancy armor

182
00:17:34,860 --> 00:17:37,480
who's better at beating little girls than fighting men.

183
00:17:37,830 --> 00:17:40,470
Now, I have an appointment with Lord Tyrion.

184
00:17:40,470 --> 00:17:42,600
You put your hand on that door,

185
00:17:43,300 --> 00:17:45,000
you lose the hand.

186
00:18:01,940 --> 00:18:04,500
As much as I appreciate a walk in the sunshine, your lordship,

187
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:06,420
I am wondering why you sent for me.

188
00:18:06,420 --> 00:18:08,750
A number of people in this city want to kill me.

189
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:10,200
You're here to protect me.

190
00:18:10,770 --> 00:18:12,530
I've been doing that for a while now.

191
00:18:12,530 --> 00:18:14,090
Do you grow bored protecting me?

192
00:18:14,090 --> 00:18:15,670
I grow poor protecting you.

193
00:18:15,670 --> 00:18:17,750
Poor? Poor?

194
00:18:17,890 --> 00:18:19,750
Under my patronage you've become a knight,

195
00:18:19,750 --> 00:18:21,750
you've served as Commander of the City Watch.

196
00:18:21,750 --> 00:18:24,520
- Briefly. - I'm sure you filled your pockets.

197
00:18:24,540 --> 00:18:26,290
And now my pockets are empty.

198
00:18:26,720 --> 00:18:29,010
You've given me a taste for the finer things.

199
00:18:29,010 --> 00:18:31,170
And if you want me to carry on protecting you,

200
00:18:31,270 --> 00:18:32,590
you'll need to pay more.

201
00:18:32,590 --> 00:18:34,730
- I thought we were friends. - We are.

202
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:37,720
But I'm a sellsword. I sell my sword.

203
00:18:37,720 --> 00:18:39,640
I don't loan it out to friends as a favor.

204
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:41,010
- How much? - Double.

205
00:18:41,010 --> 00:18:42,940
- Double? - I'm a knight now.

206
00:18:43,250 --> 00:18:44,590
Knights are worth double.

207
00:18:44,590 --> 00:18:46,920
I don't even know how much I'm paying you now.

208
00:18:47,150 --> 00:18:48,830
Which means you can afford it.

209
00:19:27,430 --> 00:19:29,280
Here. Here!

210
00:19:38,690 --> 00:19:40,350
Help me!

211
00:20:03,470 --> 00:20:04,590
Who are you?

212
00:20:06,950 --> 00:20:10,970
I was in the battle at Blackwater.

213
00:20:12,590 --> 00:20:16,030
I was a captain and a knight.

214
00:20:16,290 --> 00:20:19,630
Aye, Ser, and serving which king?

215
00:20:25,860 --> 00:20:27,890
The one true king of Westeros--

216
00:20:31,130 --> 00:20:32,670
Stannis Baratheon.

217
00:20:42,790 --> 00:20:44,260
I thought you were dead.

218
00:20:44,560 --> 00:20:46,510
Everyone thought you were dead.

219
00:20:51,670 --> 00:20:52,990
And your son?

220
00:20:59,210 --> 00:21:01,190
He may have swam ashore as you did.

221
00:21:01,190 --> 00:21:03,490
No, the wildfire took him. I saw it.

222
00:21:13,650 --> 00:21:15,390
I'm so sorry, my friend.

223
00:21:16,910 --> 00:21:18,570
I, too, have lost a son.

224
00:21:19,470 --> 00:21:21,400
There is nothing worse in this world.

225
00:21:23,210 --> 00:21:26,540
But, Davos, you were a good father.

226
00:21:27,660 --> 00:21:29,910
If I was a good father, he'd still be here.

227
00:21:33,170 --> 00:21:34,590
Stannis lives?

228
00:21:34,740 --> 00:21:37,000
He licks his wounds at Dragonstone.

229
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,440
Will you take me there?

230
00:21:38,540 --> 00:21:40,900
There is nothing for me at Dragonstone.

231
00:21:40,910 --> 00:21:42,570
This war is not over.

232
00:21:42,570 --> 00:21:43,910
Not for you, maybe.

233
00:21:43,910 --> 00:21:47,080
But for Salladhor Saan, the war is over.

234
00:21:47,330 --> 00:21:48,920
We're both sworn to King Stannis.

235
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:50,890
I am sworn to no man.

236
00:21:51,230 --> 00:21:55,210
I promised you 30 ships and you promised me riches and glory.

237
00:21:55,210 --> 00:21:56,650
I delivered the ships.

238
00:21:56,650 --> 00:21:58,800
Stannis never gives up. Never.

239
00:21:58,810 --> 00:22:01,160
- Now he will regroup. - He's a broken man.

240
00:22:01,220 --> 00:22:03,810
His fleet lies at the bottom of Blackwater Bay.

241
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:05,370
They say he sees no one--

242
00:22:05,370 --> 00:22:07,630
not his generals, not even his wife.

243
00:22:07,630 --> 00:22:09,530
Only the Red Woman

244
00:22:11,120 --> 00:22:12,310
whispering in his ear,

245
00:22:12,310 --> 00:22:14,290
telling him what she sees in the flames

246
00:22:15,200 --> 00:22:16,940
and burning men alive.

247
00:22:16,990 --> 00:22:17,960
What?

248
00:22:17,970 --> 00:22:20,740
They built a great fire when Stannis returned.

249
00:22:21,870 --> 00:22:27,250
All those who spoke against her she called servants of darkness.

250
00:22:29,270 --> 00:22:31,570
They say she sang to them as they burned.

251
00:22:36,770 --> 00:22:38,150
I'm a pirate.

252
00:22:38,650 --> 00:22:40,030
You're a smuggler.

253
00:22:40,410 --> 00:22:41,930
Servants of darkness.

254
00:22:42,940 --> 00:22:45,950
I'm thinking Dragonstone is a good place for us to avoid.

255
00:22:45,950 --> 00:22:47,580
Take me back there, please.

256
00:22:48,130 --> 00:22:49,990
You cannot turn Stannis against her.

257
00:22:49,990 --> 00:22:52,320
Maybe not, but I could carve her heart out.

258
00:22:52,320 --> 00:22:53,910
You could try.

259
00:22:53,970 --> 00:22:56,550
If you fail, they will burn you.

260
00:22:56,630 --> 00:22:59,110
If you succeed, they'll burn you.

261
00:22:59,440 --> 00:23:01,260
And you've only just come back to life.

262
00:23:01,650 --> 00:23:03,680
Stay alive a little longer, my friend.

263
00:23:03,970 --> 00:23:06,840
You call me friend. You drank with me on my wedding day.

264
00:23:06,840 --> 00:23:09,200
And you drank with me on four of my wedding days,

265
00:23:09,210 --> 00:23:10,870
but I don't ask you for favors.

266
00:23:10,870 --> 00:23:12,450
I have to stop her.

267
00:23:12,450 --> 00:23:15,350
Please, do this for me.

268
00:23:18,830 --> 00:23:20,220
When you are dead,

269
00:23:20,850 --> 00:23:23,190
I will gather your bones in a little sack

270
00:23:23,510 --> 00:23:26,440
and let your widow wear them around her neck.

271
00:23:39,460 --> 00:23:42,420
We should set the siege lines 1,000 yards from Harrenhal.

272
00:23:42,770 --> 00:23:45,620
There won't be a siege. The Mountain can't defend a ruin.

273
00:23:45,620 --> 00:23:47,180
I imagine the Mountain will defend

274
00:23:47,180 --> 00:23:49,040
whatever Tywin Lannister tells him to defend.

275
00:23:49,040 --> 00:23:51,440
The Lannisters have been running from us since Oxcross.

276
00:23:51,440 --> 00:23:52,640
I'd love a fight.

277
00:23:52,640 --> 00:23:54,440
The men would love a fight.

278
00:23:55,110 --> 00:23:57,070
I don't think we're going to get one.

279
00:24:44,740 --> 00:24:49,030
200 Northmen slaughtered like sheep.

280
00:24:49,610 --> 00:24:51,700
The debt will be repaid, my friend.

281
00:24:52,250 --> 00:24:54,750
For them and for your sons.

282
00:24:55,210 --> 00:24:56,190
Will it?

283
00:24:57,250 --> 00:24:59,450
They rot in the ground

284
00:24:59,450 --> 00:25:01,420
while their killer runs free.

285
00:25:02,090 --> 00:25:04,630
The Kingslayer won't remain free for long.

286
00:25:05,020 --> 00:25:06,660
My best hunters are after him.

287
00:25:26,730 --> 00:25:29,980
- The Mallister? - Ser Jeremy.

288
00:25:30,840 --> 00:25:32,710
My father's bannerman.

289
00:25:53,420 --> 00:25:55,880
Find her a chamber that will serve as a cell.

290
00:26:08,480 --> 00:26:09,960
She's your mother.

291
00:26:09,960 --> 00:26:11,900
She freed Jaime Lannister.

292
00:26:12,730 --> 00:26:14,870
The Lannisters robbed them of their sons

293
00:26:14,880 --> 00:26:16,900
and she robbed them of their justice.

294
00:26:19,080 --> 00:26:20,100
Water.

295
00:26:22,680 --> 00:26:23,630
Water.

296
00:26:23,920 --> 00:26:25,850
This needs to be cleaned and closed.

297
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:32,530
What's your name, friend?

298
00:26:33,140 --> 00:26:34,310
Qyburn.

299
00:26:34,730 --> 00:26:36,310
You're lucky to be alive.

300
00:26:39,420 --> 00:26:40,480
Lucky?

301
00:27:07,840 --> 00:27:09,470
The badge looks good on you.

302
00:27:11,850 --> 00:27:13,840
Almost as good as it looked on me.

303
00:27:16,610 --> 00:27:18,780
Are you enjoying your new position?

304
00:27:21,380 --> 00:27:22,810
Am I enjoying it?

305
00:27:22,810 --> 00:27:24,640
I was very happy as Hand of the King.

306
00:27:26,320 --> 00:27:27,310
Yes.

307
00:27:27,320 --> 00:27:29,410
I heard how happy you were.

308
00:27:31,170 --> 00:27:34,000
You brought a whore into my bed.

309
00:27:34,490 --> 00:27:36,420
It wasn't your bed at the time.

310
00:27:39,210 --> 00:27:41,570
I sent you here to advise the king.

311
00:27:42,460 --> 00:27:45,830
I gave you real power and authority.

312
00:27:46,230 --> 00:27:50,150
You chose to spend your days as you always have,

313
00:27:50,740 --> 00:27:52,330
bedding harlots

314
00:27:53,110 --> 00:27:55,340
and drinking with thieves.

315
00:27:57,560 --> 00:27:59,890
Occasionally I drank with the harlots.

316
00:28:00,150 --> 00:28:02,150
What do you want, Tyrion?

317
00:28:02,150 --> 00:28:04,780
Why does everyone assume I want something?

318
00:28:05,410 --> 00:28:07,730
Can't I simply visit with my beloved father?

319
00:28:09,350 --> 00:28:10,840
My beloved father who

320
00:28:12,030 --> 00:28:14,960
somehow forgot to visit his wounded son

321
00:28:14,960 --> 00:28:16,640
after he fell on the battlefield.

322
00:28:16,640 --> 00:28:20,140
Maester Pycelle assured me your wounds were not fatal.

323
00:28:20,140 --> 00:28:22,430
I organized the defense of this city

324
00:28:23,390 --> 00:28:25,620
while you held court in the ruins of Harrenhal.

325
00:28:26,700 --> 00:28:29,070
I led the foray when the enemies were at the gate

326
00:28:29,070 --> 00:28:31,300
while your grandson, the king,

327
00:28:31,550 --> 00:28:33,950
quivered in fear behind the walls.

328
00:28:34,760 --> 00:28:37,860
I bled in the mud for our family.

329
00:28:38,680 --> 00:28:40,120
And as my reward,

330
00:28:40,540 --> 00:28:42,590
I was trundled off to some dark little cell.

331
00:28:44,120 --> 00:28:45,360
But what do I want?

332
00:28:46,820 --> 00:28:49,020
A little bloody gratitude would be a start.

333
00:28:49,500 --> 00:28:52,400
Jugglers and singers require applause.

334
00:28:52,810 --> 00:28:54,560
You are a Lannister.

335
00:28:55,880 --> 00:28:57,770
Do you think I demanded a garland of roses

336
00:28:57,770 --> 00:29:00,480
every time I suffered a wound on a battlefield?

337
00:29:02,930 --> 00:29:06,190
Now, I have seven kingdoms to look after

338
00:29:06,770 --> 00:29:08,940
and three of them are in open rebellion.

339
00:29:08,940 --> 00:29:13,690
So tell me what you want.

340
00:29:17,760 --> 00:29:20,270
I want what is mine by right.

341
00:29:22,140 --> 00:29:24,130
Jaime is your eldest son,

342
00:29:24,130 --> 00:29:25,550
heir to your lands and titles.

343
00:29:25,900 --> 00:29:27,190
But he is a Kingsguard,

344
00:29:27,190 --> 00:29:29,230
forbidden from marriage or inheritance.

345
00:29:29,860 --> 00:29:31,700
The day Jaime put on the white cloak,

346
00:29:32,230 --> 00:29:34,610
he gave up his claim to Casterly Rock.

347
00:29:35,940 --> 00:29:38,590
I am your son and lawful heir.

348
00:29:41,730 --> 00:29:43,250
You want Casterly Rock?

349
00:29:43,250 --> 00:29:45,180
It is mine by right.

350
00:29:50,310 --> 00:29:52,130
We'll find you accommodations

351
00:29:52,290 --> 00:29:54,160
more suited to your name

352
00:29:54,380 --> 00:29:56,400
and as a reward for your accomplishments

353
00:29:56,400 --> 00:29:59,130
during the battle of Blackwater Bay.

354
00:30:00,770 --> 00:30:03,130
And when the time is right, you will be given a position

355
00:30:03,130 --> 00:30:04,720
fit for your talents

356
00:30:05,060 --> 00:30:07,240
so that you can serve your family

357
00:30:07,240 --> 00:30:09,090
and protect our legacy.

358
00:30:10,030 --> 00:30:11,200
And if you serve faithfully,

359
00:30:11,200 --> 00:30:13,610
you will be rewarded with a suitable wife.

360
00:30:14,910 --> 00:30:17,310
And I would let myself be consumed by maggots

361
00:30:17,310 --> 00:30:18,910
before mocking the family name

362
00:30:18,910 --> 00:30:21,700
and making you heir to Casterly Rock.

363
00:30:23,700 --> 00:30:25,430
- Why? - Why?

364
00:30:26,410 --> 00:30:27,730
You ask that?

365
00:30:28,660 --> 00:30:31,330
You, who killed your mother to come into the world?

366
00:30:31,960 --> 00:30:35,420
You are an ill-made, spiteful little creature

367
00:30:36,070 --> 00:30:39,450
full of envy, lust, and low cunning.

368
00:30:40,340 --> 00:30:42,820
Men's laws give you the right to bear my name

369
00:30:42,820 --> 00:30:44,270
and display my colors

370
00:30:44,270 --> 00:30:47,420
since I cannot prove that you are not mine.

371
00:30:48,850 --> 00:30:51,340
And to teach me humility, the Gods have condemned me

372
00:30:51,340 --> 00:30:54,800
to watch you waddle about wearing that proud lion

373
00:30:54,800 --> 00:30:58,180
that was my father's sigil and his father's before him.

374
00:30:58,940 --> 00:31:00,570
But neither Gods nor men

375
00:31:00,570 --> 00:31:03,600
will ever compel me to let you turn Casterly Rock

376
00:31:03,600 --> 00:31:05,100
into your whorehouse.

377
00:31:07,040 --> 00:31:08,830
Go, now.

378
00:31:12,630 --> 00:31:16,310
Speak no more of your rights to Casterly Rock.

379
00:31:18,520 --> 00:31:19,420
Go.

380
00:31:29,620 --> 00:31:30,950
Oh, one more thing.

381
00:31:34,080 --> 00:31:36,970
The next whore I catch in your bed I'll hang.

382
00:31:45,190 --> 00:31:47,840
Dorne. It's going to Dorne.

383
00:31:48,030 --> 00:31:50,670
- Why Dorne? - It's carrying silk

384
00:31:50,930 --> 00:31:54,180
and it's supposed to bring back wine in exchange.

385
00:31:58,800 --> 00:32:00,510
But it's not coming back.

386
00:32:00,990 --> 00:32:03,240
The captain's tired of risking his life

387
00:32:03,240 --> 00:32:05,500
so King's Landing lords and ladies

388
00:32:05,500 --> 00:32:08,270
can get drunk on better wine than they deserve.

389
00:32:10,010 --> 00:32:11,750
He's going to stay in Dorne.

390
00:32:12,190 --> 00:32:14,540
Wait out the winter where it's beautiful and warm.

391
00:32:15,780 --> 00:32:19,230
I met some people in Dorne who weren't so beautiful and warm.

392
00:32:19,510 --> 00:32:20,850
Don't ruin the game.

393
00:32:21,860 --> 00:32:23,620
I told you, I don't want to play.

394
00:32:25,390 --> 00:32:26,800
What about that one there?

395
00:32:27,360 --> 00:32:28,310
That one?

396
00:32:28,970 --> 00:32:30,370
It's going to Volantis.

397
00:32:30,780 --> 00:32:31,360
Why?

398
00:32:32,220 --> 00:32:35,530
Because when I got on a ship in Volantis, it looked like that one.

399
00:32:36,820 --> 00:32:38,460
That's not how the game works.

400
00:32:38,460 --> 00:32:41,680
You're not supposed to just blurt out the right answer.

401
00:32:42,070 --> 00:32:43,530
You've got to invent a story

402
00:32:43,530 --> 00:32:46,460
about where the ship is going and why.

403
00:32:47,300 --> 00:32:50,070
Why should I make up a story when I know the truth?

404
00:32:51,180 --> 00:32:54,740
Because the truth is always either terrible or boring.

405
00:32:54,740 --> 00:32:55,850
Lovely day for it.

406
00:32:57,910 --> 00:32:59,300
Watching the ships.

407
00:32:59,960 --> 00:33:01,060
Lord Baelish.

408
00:33:03,260 --> 00:33:07,160
Might I speak with Lady Sansa alone for a moment?

409
00:33:19,010 --> 00:33:20,940
I saw your mother not long ago.

410
00:33:23,210 --> 00:33:24,780
She's very eager to see you.

411
00:33:27,080 --> 00:33:28,250
And your sister.

412
00:33:30,560 --> 00:33:31,930
Arya's alive?

413
00:33:36,590 --> 00:33:38,060
You said you'd take me home.

414
00:33:38,710 --> 00:33:40,980
You said King's Landing was your home.

415
00:33:42,980 --> 00:33:44,100
You are the property of the crown.

416
00:33:44,100 --> 00:33:45,520
Stealing you would be treason.

417
00:33:45,520 --> 00:33:47,390
If you were to tell just one person--

418
00:33:47,390 --> 00:33:49,630
- I won't tell anyone. - How do I know?

419
00:33:49,870 --> 00:33:51,580
Because I'm a terrible liar.

420
00:33:52,220 --> 00:33:53,600
You said so yourself.

421
00:33:54,750 --> 00:33:55,760
Please, Lord Baelish.

422
00:33:55,760 --> 00:33:57,360
Tell me what to do. Tell me when.

423
00:34:00,900 --> 00:34:02,590
I'm waiting for word on an assignment

424
00:34:02,590 --> 00:34:04,470
that will take me far away from the capital.

425
00:34:05,860 --> 00:34:07,040
When I set sail,

426
00:34:07,490 --> 00:34:09,620
I might be able to take you with me.

427
00:34:10,310 --> 00:34:12,830
But you'll need to be ready to leave on a moment's notice.

428
00:34:15,590 --> 00:34:16,850
You're her handmaiden?

429
00:34:20,150 --> 00:34:22,780
Yes. And you're his...?

430
00:34:23,060 --> 00:34:24,600
I help manage his affairs.

431
00:34:26,380 --> 00:34:29,400
- He's an important person. - So is she.

432
00:34:29,640 --> 00:34:31,700
I grew up in the shadow of her father's castle.

433
00:34:32,510 --> 00:34:34,070
The day she was born, they rang the bells

434
00:34:34,070 --> 00:34:35,920
from sunrise till sunset.

435
00:34:39,020 --> 00:34:41,110
We've both done rather well, you and I.

436
00:34:44,460 --> 00:34:45,330
Yes.

437
00:34:46,020 --> 00:34:47,600
Given where we started.

438
00:34:49,530 --> 00:34:50,950
And where is that?

439
00:34:53,100 --> 00:34:56,470
It's not easy for girls like us to dig our way out.

440
00:35:02,110 --> 00:35:03,210
Watch out for her.

441
00:35:04,960 --> 00:35:06,490
I always do.

442
00:35:08,140 --> 00:35:09,650
Watch out for her with him.

443
00:36:03,030 --> 00:36:04,280
They're growing fast.

444
00:36:08,000 --> 00:36:09,330
Not fast enough.

445
00:36:10,670 --> 00:36:11,740
I can't wait that long.

446
00:36:16,050 --> 00:36:17,260
I need an army.

447
00:36:18,920 --> 00:36:20,880
We'll be in Astapor by nightfall.

448
00:36:22,700 --> 00:36:25,750
Some say the Unsullied are the greatest soldiers in the world.

449
00:36:26,290 --> 00:36:28,220
The greatest slave-soldiers in the world.

450
00:36:28,420 --> 00:36:30,590
The distinction means a good deal to some people.

451
00:36:30,590 --> 00:36:32,640
Do those people have any better ideas

452
00:36:32,640 --> 00:36:34,590
about how to put you on the Iron Throne?

453
00:36:37,650 --> 00:36:39,260
It's too beautiful a day to argue.

454
00:36:43,130 --> 00:36:43,910
You're right.

455
00:36:47,370 --> 00:36:49,660
Another lovely day on the high seas.

456
00:36:49,860 --> 00:36:51,310
Don't mock them.

457
00:36:51,850 --> 00:36:54,100
They're the first Dothraki who have ever been on a ship.

458
00:36:54,100 --> 00:36:56,560
They followed me across the poison water.

459
00:36:56,560 --> 00:36:57,900
If they'll do it, others will.

460
00:36:57,900 --> 00:36:59,150
And with a true Khalasar--

461
00:36:59,150 --> 00:37:02,900
The Dothraki follow strength above all, Khaleesi.

462
00:37:03,700 --> 00:37:06,940
You'll have a true Khalasar when you prove yourself strong.

463
00:37:07,700 --> 00:37:08,990
And not before.

464
00:37:36,850 --> 00:37:37,810
Your Grace.

465
00:37:49,550 --> 00:37:51,000
I heard you were dead.

466
00:37:52,320 --> 00:37:53,120
Not yet.

467
00:37:56,120 --> 00:37:58,860
I had hoped to speak to you alone, Your Grace.

468
00:37:59,890 --> 00:38:01,050
We are alone.

469
00:38:12,270 --> 00:38:14,450
Your Grace, you are the rightful king.

470
00:38:15,490 --> 00:38:16,710
Not only by blood.

471
00:38:17,920 --> 00:38:19,950
You're an honorable man, a just man.

472
00:38:21,290 --> 00:38:22,900
And there is still a war to fight.

473
00:38:23,820 --> 00:38:25,020
I am fighting.

474
00:38:26,300 --> 00:38:28,150
By burning prisoners alive?

475
00:38:30,730 --> 00:38:32,790
How would you punish the infidels, Ser Davos?

476
00:38:32,790 --> 00:38:35,490
I do not judge people for the gods they worship.

477
00:38:35,490 --> 00:38:37,390
If I did, I'd have thrown you in the sea

478
00:38:37,390 --> 00:38:39,900
before you ever set foot on Dragonstone.

479
00:38:40,350 --> 00:38:42,670
- I'm not your enemy. - You are my enemy.

480
00:38:47,280 --> 00:38:49,110
Was it me you fought on Blackwater Bay?

481
00:38:50,810 --> 00:38:52,530
Did I set your ships ablaze?

482
00:38:56,790 --> 00:39:00,500
I wasn't there when the wildfire killed our men by the thousands.

483
00:39:02,930 --> 00:39:04,370
I could have saved those men.

484
00:39:05,690 --> 00:39:06,950
You would have taken the city,

485
00:39:06,950 --> 00:39:08,980
Stannis would now sit upon his rightful throne,

486
00:39:08,980 --> 00:39:10,520
and you would stand beside him.

487
00:39:11,690 --> 00:39:12,850
But I wasn't there

488
00:39:13,510 --> 00:39:16,750
because you convinced your king to leave me behind.

489
00:39:25,320 --> 00:39:26,960
Do you hear them screaming?

490
00:39:28,390 --> 00:39:30,800
All those burning men in the water

491
00:39:31,960 --> 00:39:34,010
crying for their mothers,

492
00:39:34,170 --> 00:39:36,360
for their gods for help?

493
00:39:37,180 --> 00:39:39,610
Until the moment the Blackwater swallowed them.

494
00:39:46,750 --> 00:39:48,540
Don't despair, Ser Davos.

495
00:39:49,600 --> 00:39:51,110
What I told your son is true.

496
00:39:52,350 --> 00:39:56,000
Death by fire is the purest death.

497
00:39:58,730 --> 00:39:59,670
This woman is evil!

498
00:40:00,230 --> 00:40:01,920
She's the mother of demons.

499
00:40:02,170 --> 00:40:04,130
Take him to the dungeon and lock him in a cell.

500
00:40:04,130 --> 00:40:05,580
- Your Grace! - Come on.

501
00:40:05,580 --> 00:40:07,260
You've chosen the darkness, Ser Davos.

502
00:40:07,260 --> 00:40:09,920
- She will destroy us all! - I will pray for you.

503
00:40:10,650 --> 00:40:11,790
Your Grace!

504
00:40:39,980 --> 00:40:41,950
Halt. Down.

505
00:40:43,320 --> 00:40:45,610
Halt. Down.

506
00:40:52,570 --> 00:40:53,580
Why have we stopped?

507
00:40:53,760 --> 00:40:55,490
It's Lady Margaery, Your Grace.

508
00:41:01,130 --> 00:41:02,930
What is she doing? Who gave her permission?

509
00:41:03,360 --> 00:41:06,600
My lady. We should have guards, my lady.

510
00:41:06,810 --> 00:41:07,350
Why?

511
00:41:12,250 --> 00:41:13,170
Pardon me.

512
00:41:21,060 --> 00:41:23,920
Stop, my lady. You'll ruin your dress.

513
00:41:24,650 --> 00:41:25,690
I have others.

514
00:41:32,220 --> 00:41:34,180
Would you like to speak with her, Your Grace?

515
00:41:37,610 --> 00:41:38,190
No.

516
00:41:39,190 --> 00:41:40,270
He was a soldier.

517
00:41:41,520 --> 00:41:42,820
He went to fight on the walls

518
00:41:43,300 --> 00:41:44,830
when the ships came into Blackwater Bay.

519
00:41:46,230 --> 00:41:47,630
He never came back.

520
00:41:48,090 --> 00:41:49,110
And your mother?

521
00:41:50,040 --> 00:41:51,440
She died when she had me.

522
00:41:54,900 --> 00:41:57,060
Bad men wanted to come into this city

523
00:41:57,060 --> 00:42:00,650
and do terrible things, but your father stopped them.

524
00:42:07,070 --> 00:42:08,760
Whenever you look at this knight,

525
00:42:09,120 --> 00:42:11,090
I want you to remember your father.

526
00:42:14,340 --> 00:42:15,800
He wasn't a knight.

527
00:42:16,410 --> 00:42:17,900
He was just a soldier.

528
00:42:18,280 --> 00:42:19,910
And what do knights swear to do?

529
00:42:20,850 --> 00:42:23,540
Protect the weak and uphold the good.

530
00:42:24,210 --> 00:42:27,280
Your father did that. Be proud of him.

531
00:42:30,700 --> 00:42:32,700
Was your father a soldier, too?

532
00:42:34,460 --> 00:42:36,480
You should be proud, too.

533
00:42:39,370 --> 00:42:41,690
Under King Joffrey's leadership,

534
00:42:41,690 --> 00:42:44,300
your fathers saved the city.

535
00:42:44,890 --> 00:42:46,120
They saved us all.

536
00:42:46,800 --> 00:42:50,000
From now on, we're going to take care of you.

537
00:42:52,790 --> 00:42:53,630
All of you.

538
00:43:01,760 --> 00:43:04,860
Come to me for whatever you need to feed them, clothe them, or house them.

539
00:43:07,440 --> 00:43:09,160
Directly to me.

540
00:43:24,760 --> 00:43:26,750
- Your Grace. - Your Grace.

541
00:43:26,750 --> 00:43:28,200
Please, sit. Sit.

542
00:43:28,200 --> 00:43:30,150
I do apologize, my lady.

543
00:43:30,700 --> 00:43:32,690
Small council meetings.

544
00:43:33,180 --> 00:43:36,940
At what point does it become treason to waste the king's time?

545
00:43:41,790 --> 00:43:43,320
That's a lovely gown, my lady.

546
00:43:43,320 --> 00:43:45,040
Yes, it suits you perfectly.

547
00:43:45,640 --> 00:43:47,510
I imagine you might be rather cold.

548
00:43:47,880 --> 00:43:51,340
The climate is a bit more forgiving back in Highgarden, Your Grace.

549
00:43:51,580 --> 00:43:53,840
Shall I have them bring you a shawl, my lady?

550
00:43:54,610 --> 00:43:56,840
I am touched by your concern, Your Grace.

551
00:43:57,170 --> 00:44:00,480
Luckily for us Tyrells, our blood runs quite warm.

552
00:44:00,480 --> 00:44:02,570
- Doesn't it, Loras? - Yes.

553
00:44:02,570 --> 00:44:05,440
Loras, isn't the queen's gown magnificent?

554
00:44:06,130 --> 00:44:08,770
The fabric, the embroidery, the metalwork.

555
00:44:08,770 --> 00:44:10,430
I've never seen anything like it.

556
00:44:10,430 --> 00:44:12,420
You might find a bit of armor quite useful

557
00:44:12,420 --> 00:44:14,710
once you become queen. Perhaps before.

558
00:44:15,680 --> 00:44:18,720
Joffrey tells me you stopped your carriage at Flea Bottom

559
00:44:18,720 --> 00:44:20,580
on your way back from the Sept this morning.

560
00:44:21,010 --> 00:44:26,010
Yes. I paid a visit to an orphanage the High Septon told me about.

561
00:44:26,650 --> 00:44:29,420
Margaery does a great deal of work with the poor back in Highgarden.

562
00:44:30,200 --> 00:44:31,240
The lowest among us are

563
00:44:31,240 --> 00:44:33,800
no different from the highest if you give them a chance

564
00:44:33,800 --> 00:44:35,800
and approach them with an open heart.

565
00:44:35,800 --> 00:44:37,820
An open heart is what you'll get in Flea Bottom

566
00:44:37,820 --> 00:44:39,420
if you're not careful, my dear.

567
00:44:39,910 --> 00:44:42,580
Not long ago, we were attacked by a mob there.

568
00:44:43,800 --> 00:44:46,400
We had a full complement of guards that didn't stop them.

569
00:44:47,530 --> 00:44:49,240
The king barely escaped with his life.

570
00:44:49,390 --> 00:44:52,320
My mother's always had a penchant for drama.

571
00:44:53,250 --> 00:44:57,490
Facts become less and less important to her as she grows older.

572
00:44:57,890 --> 00:45:00,120
Our lives were never truly in danger.

573
00:45:02,120 --> 00:45:03,490
You're right, of course.

574
00:45:03,850 --> 00:45:05,330
But you are your father's son.

575
00:45:06,790 --> 00:45:08,700
We can't all have a king's bravery.

576
00:45:17,390 --> 00:45:19,640
Hunger turns men into beasts.

577
00:45:20,100 --> 00:45:23,220
I'm glad House Tyrell has been able to help in this regard.

578
00:45:23,580 --> 00:45:27,010
They tell me 100 wagons arrive daily now from the Reach.

579
00:45:27,010 --> 00:45:30,500
Wheat, barley, apples. We've had a blessed harvest.

580
00:45:30,500 --> 00:45:34,680
And, of course, it's our duty to assist the capital in time of need.

581
00:45:35,700 --> 00:45:37,220
Well, as Ser Loras said,

582
00:45:37,220 --> 00:45:39,400
Lady Margaery has done this sort of...

583
00:45:40,610 --> 00:45:42,590
charitable work before.

584
00:45:43,470 --> 00:45:44,960
I'm sure she knows what she's doing.

585
00:45:47,060 --> 00:45:48,460
I'm sure she does.

586
00:46:17,550 --> 00:46:20,350
The Unsullied have stood here for a day and a night

587
00:46:20,350 --> 00:46:22,190
with no food or water.

588
00:46:28,700 --> 00:46:30,420
They will stand until they drop.

589
00:46:32,880 --> 00:46:34,930
Such is their obedience.

590
00:46:37,170 --> 00:46:38,640
They may suit my needs.

591
00:46:39,290 --> 00:46:40,560
Tell me of their training.

592
00:47:01,250 --> 00:47:03,330
They begin their training at five.

593
00:47:03,790 --> 00:47:05,950
Every day they drill from dawn to dusk

594
00:47:05,950 --> 00:47:08,170
until they have mastered the shortsword,

595
00:47:08,170 --> 00:47:10,320
the shield, and the three spears.

596
00:47:10,860 --> 00:47:14,000
Only one boy in four survives this rigorous training.

597
00:47:16,400 --> 00:47:19,510
Their discipline and loyalty are absolute.

598
00:47:20,330 --> 00:47:21,990
They fear nothing.

599
00:47:22,270 --> 00:47:24,530
Even the bravest men fear death.

600
00:47:46,240 --> 00:47:48,550
My master says the Unsullied are not men.

601
00:47:49,170 --> 00:47:50,920
Death means nothing to them.

602
00:48:00,180 --> 00:48:02,770
He begs you attend to this carefully, Your Grace.

603
00:48:17,250 --> 00:48:19,690
Tell the good master there is no need.

604
00:48:27,560 --> 00:48:30,530
My master points out that men don't need nipples.

605
00:48:46,810 --> 00:48:48,580
To win his shield,

606
00:48:48,580 --> 00:48:51,850
an Unsullied must go to the slave marts with a silver mark,

607
00:48:52,650 --> 00:48:56,940
find a newborn and kill it before its mother's eyes.

608
00:48:59,890 --> 00:49:02,220
This way, my master says, we make certain

609
00:49:02,220 --> 00:49:04,120
there is no weakness left in them.

610
00:49:05,300 --> 00:49:07,910
You take a babe from its mother's arms,

611
00:49:08,310 --> 00:49:10,100
kill it as she watches,

612
00:49:10,100 --> 00:49:12,330
and pay for her pain with a silver coin?

613
00:49:26,860 --> 00:49:29,160
My master would like you to know that the silver is paid

614
00:49:29,160 --> 00:49:31,430
to the baby's owner, not the mother.

615
00:49:38,050 --> 00:49:39,860
How many do you have to sell?

616
00:49:45,420 --> 00:49:46,760
8,000.

617
00:49:51,620 --> 00:49:54,210
Master Kraznys asks that you please hurry.

618
00:49:54,210 --> 00:49:56,680
Many other buyers are interested.

619
00:50:07,310 --> 00:50:10,140
8,000 dead babies.

620
00:50:10,580 --> 00:50:12,520
The Unsullied are a means to an end.

621
00:50:13,490 --> 00:50:15,560
Once I own them, these men--

622
00:50:15,560 --> 00:50:17,760
They're not men. Not anymore.

623
00:50:18,410 --> 00:50:21,460
Once I own an army of slaves, what will I be?

624
00:50:21,460 --> 00:50:23,840
Do you think these slaves will have better lives

625
00:50:23,840 --> 00:50:26,930
serving Kraznys and men like him or serving you?

626
00:50:41,020 --> 00:50:42,220
You'll be fair to them.

627
00:50:42,530 --> 00:50:44,610
You won't mutilate them to make a point.

628
00:50:50,060 --> 00:50:52,100
You won't order them to murder babies.

629
00:50:52,100 --> 00:50:54,140
You'll see they're properly fed and sheltered.

630
00:50:54,950 --> 00:50:57,300
A great injustice has been done to them.

631
00:50:58,960 --> 00:51:00,760
Closing your eyes will not undo it.

632
00:51:58,170 --> 00:51:59,500
The warlocks.

633
00:52:03,600 --> 00:52:05,510
I owe you my life, ser.

634
00:52:06,460 --> 00:52:07,680
The honor is mine,

635
00:52:08,580 --> 00:52:09,550
my queen.

636
00:52:13,920 --> 00:52:15,030
You know this man?

637
00:52:16,050 --> 00:52:17,250
I know him

638
00:52:17,960 --> 00:52:21,100
as one of the greatest fighters the Seven Kingdoms has ever seen

639
00:52:22,320 --> 00:52:26,480
and as the Lord Commander of Robert Baratheon's Kingsguard.

640
00:52:28,110 --> 00:52:29,430
King Robert is dead.

641
00:52:30,210 --> 00:52:32,780
I have been searching for you, Daenerys Stormborn,

642
00:52:33,220 --> 00:52:34,670
to ask your forgiveness.

643
00:52:35,840 --> 00:52:37,790
I was sworn to protect your family.

644
00:52:40,240 --> 00:52:41,350
I failed them.

645
00:52:47,720 --> 00:52:49,500
I am Barristan Selmy,

646
00:52:50,190 --> 00:52:51,810
Kingsguard to your father.

647
00:52:52,480 --> 00:52:54,310
Allow me to join your Queensguard

648
00:52:55,290 --> 00:52:57,340
and I will not fail you again.

